title: >-
  de-Ferra2020-kz: A REMARK reproducing Household Heterogeneity
  and the Transmission of Foreign Shocks
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-04-04'
authors:
  - given-names: Siying
    family-names: Li
    affiliation: Johns Hopkins University
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Siying99/de-Ferra2020-kz'
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  REMARK (Replication and Exploration Made using ARK) for
  de Ferra, Mitman, and Romei (2020), "Household heterogeneity
  and the transmission of foreign shocks," Journal of
  International Economics 124, 103303. The repository includes
  (1) a LaTeX paper summarising the HANKSOME model, calibration,
  and main results; (2) a Python reproduction pipeline
  (notebooks 01–14) that replicates Table 1, Figures 1–5, and
  the full credit-supply expansion and unexpected-contraction
  transitions from scratch using the Rouwenhorst chain,
  Endogenous Grid Method, β-calibration, and perfect-foresight
  MIT-shock transitions under both flexible and fixed exchange
  rates; and (3) a supplementary Jupyter notebook decomposing
  the household Bellman equation into modular DDSL stages.
keywords:
  - sudden stops
  - foreign currency debt
  - exchange rate policy
  - incomplete markets
